// REJECTS: Unexpected token ','. Valid alternatives: [')']
//
// A position is exactly TWO numbers. Not a variadic coordinate list, not a tuple whose
// arity the walker checks later -- the grammar closes the paren after the second, which is
// why the only alternative offered at the third comma is ')'.
//
// Arity fixed in the grammar is the kind of thing a rewrite most easily loosens: parsing
// `(` numberList `)` and taking the first two is simpler than parsing `(` num `,` num `)`,
// handles both the position and the rectangle rules with one routine, and accepts a third
// coordinate that then vanishes without trace.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::ThreeCoordinates
{
   classView v1
   {
      class: fixture::neg::Person;
      position: (1.0,2.0,3.0);
      rectangle: (10.0,20.0);
   }
}
